From: Project Luma <builds@project-luma.local>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 12:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] luma: Dash islands on every edge, where you aim, with every setting

The owner's feedback on movable islands (ADR-044, 0167):

- Every edge takes islands, including an edge shared with another monitor
  (the sides of a middle display): those bands are reserved through
  Mutter's meta_display_set_monitor_edge_reservation() (Mutter 0016);
  without it, shared edges stay closed as before.
- A drop goes to the zone the pointer is in, wherever the island was
  grabbed; otherwise the island's centre picks the nearest zone. The
  carried island takes its target edge's form and the ghost is a preview
  group of its real length, so it is exactly where the island lands.
- Islands attach (9 px) or sit at an edge's start, centre or end; free
  positions need shelf-free-placement (Dash settings, the arrange card).
- Empty zones are drawn faint at rest and stronger with nearness, the
  target zone at full weight; each edge has a faint line that steps aside
  around every placeholder, group and ghost.
- Arranging shows the live extensions slot as a ghost island when nothing
  is live.
- Settings: Use islands off with span draws one bar along the dock's band,
  arranged groups included; Float outer edges moves the band's ends and
  squares them; Protrude keeps the windows' padding (the tiling gap on
  every edge); Keep windows out of the Dash is honoured; Position moves the
  dock's edge in an arrangement.
- Side-edge forms of the media and live islands and the column clock.
- The Dash menu is a kit menu (the app-menu presentation) and reads Dash
  Settings….
---
diff --git a/data/theme/luma-shelf.css b/data/theme/luma-shelf.css
index d961669..5c3ffd0 100644
--- a/data/theme/luma-shelf.css
+++ b/data/theme/luma-shelf.css
@@ -2352,3 +2352,57 @@ StBoxLayout.luma-notification-tray.luma-surface-dark .luma-notification-tray-cou
 .luma-surface-glass .luma-well .luma-well-extension .panel-button.screen-sharing-indicator,
 .luma-surface-glass .luma-well .luma-well-extension .panel-button.screen-recording-indicator,
 .luma-surface-glass .luma-well .luma-well-extension .panel-button.luma-screen-recorded-indicator { color: #5f3908; }
+
+/* ── Movable islands, refinements (owner, 2026-09-19) ────────────────────
+ * Zone placeholders are drawn at a weight set in code (ZONE_REST 22% at
+ * rest, rising with the pointer's nearness); the zone a drop takes is filled
+ * and loses its dashes, and the ghost (the preview group, the exact landing
+ * footprint) carries the outline, so one space holds one outline. */
+.luma-arrange-zone.luma-arrange-zone-active,
+.luma-arrange-light .luma-arrange-zone.luma-arrange-zone-active,
+.luma-arrange-frost .luma-arrange-zone.luma-arrange-zone-active,
+.luma-arrange-glass .luma-arrange-zone.luma-arrange-zone-active { -luma-line-width: 0; }
+/* The ghost of a drop on a zone: the state ink, dashed. */
+.luma-arrange-gap.luma-arrange-gap-ghost .luma-arrange-gap-footprint { color: #8a99a8; }
+.luma-arrange-gap.luma-arrange-gap-ghost.luma-arrange-light .luma-arrange-gap-footprint,
+.luma-arrange-gap.luma-arrange-gap-ghost.luma-arrange-frost .luma-arrange-gap-footprint,
+.luma-arrange-gap.luma-arrange-gap-ghost.luma-arrange-glass .luma-arrange-gap-footprint { color: #4a5a6e; }
+/* The edge line: its alpha is drawn in code (faint, brighter near the
+ * pointer); the colour is the treatment's ink. */
+.luma-arrange-edge { color: #ffffff; }
+.luma-arrange-light .luma-arrange-edge,
+.luma-arrange-frost .luma-arrange-edge,
+.luma-arrange-glass .luma-arrange-edge { color: #191b1f; }
+
+/* The live extensions slot while arranging, when no live extension runs. */
+.luma-live-ghost-outline { color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.40); -luma-line-width: 1.5px; -luma-dash: 5; border-radius: 15px; }
+.luma-live-ghost-content { spacing: 8px; padding: 0 14px; }
+.luma-live-ghost-icon { icon-size: 16px; color: rgba(231, 233, 232, 0.62); }
+.luma-live-ghost-label { font-family: Figtree, sans-serif; font-size: 12px; font-weight: 600; color: rgba(231, 233, 232, 0.62); }
+.luma-live-ghost.luma-arrange-light .luma-live-ghost-outline,
+.luma-live-ghost.luma-arrange-frost .luma-live-ghost-outline,
+.luma-live-ghost.luma-arrange-glass .luma-live-ghost-outline { color: rgba(25, 27, 31, 0.36); }
+.luma-live-ghost.luma-arrange-light .luma-live-ghost-label,
+.luma-live-ghost.luma-arrange-frost .luma-live-ghost-label,
+.luma-live-ghost.luma-arrange-glass .luma-live-ghost-label,
+.luma-live-ghost.luma-arrange-light .luma-live-ghost-icon,
+.luma-live-ghost.luma-arrange-frost .luma-live-ghost-icon,
+.luma-live-ghost.luma-arrange-glass .luma-live-ghost-icon { color: rgba(25, 27, 31, 0.62); }
+
+/* Allow free placement, in the arrange card. */
+.luma-arrange-option { padding: 6px 0 12px; }
+.luma-arrange-option-label { font-size: 12px; font-weight: 600; }
+
+/* Menus opened from the Dash's islands are kit menus: the kit's 13/600
+ * Figtree rows 32 high and its rule, in every mode (the Dash menu itself
+ * uses the app-menu presentation). */
+.luma-shelf-menu .popup-menu-item { min-height: 32px; padding: 0 8px; border-radius: 10px; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 600; }
+.luma-shelf-menu .popup-separator-menu-item { min-height: 0; padding: 0; margin: 5px 4px; }
+
+/* Side-edge (column) forms of every island (ADR-044 §6). */
+.luma-shelf-vertical .luma-status-cluster .luma-status-clock,
+.luma-shelf-vertical .luma-shelf-clock-island .luma-status-clock { min-width: 0; padding: 0; }
+.luma-shelf-vertical .luma-status-cluster .luma-status-clock-text,
+.luma-shelf-vertical .luma-shelf-clock-island .luma-status-clock-text { spacing: 2px; }
+.luma-live-extension-short { font-family: Figtree, sans-serif; font-size: 11px; font-weight: 700; font-feature-settings: "tnum"; }
+.luma-shelf-vertical .luma-live-extension-content { spacing: 6px; }
